WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.412
Two things change membership
without anyone touching a rule.

2
00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:04.688
The first is a date.

3
00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:08.916
The memberOf rule preview ends
on November 3, 2026, and groups,

4
00:00:08.916 --> 00:00:14.075
units and auto-assignment policies that
use it freeze in their last state.

5
00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:18.687
So Gate 4 uses no memberOf, and
flattens nested chains instead.

6
00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:24.662
VK-DG-06 lists any rule still using it,
and any group whose processing is paused,

7
00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:30.075
because a paused group stops updating
while every other check passes.

8
00:00:30.075 --> 00:00:31.575
The second is volume.

9
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:36.935
VK-DG-05 compares each dynamic group's
member count with the snapshot from the

10
00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:42.212
last run, and flags a change of more than
ten percent and at least five members.

11
00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:46.874
The first run writes the baseline, so
take it now, before the mover proof.

12
00:00:46.874 --> 00:00:51.838
And plan for processing time: usually
a few hours, sometimes more than a day.

13
00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:56.980
For a bulk change, pause nonessential
groups for a day, then resume in phases.
